From: atomchild411 <143453386+atomchild411@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:05:00 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Style: a custom property equals itself without comparing values

CustomPropertyData::operator== (deduplicateCustomProperties, at each
restyled element) compares every custom property of two sets, through
CustomProperty::operator==: names, then values in depth. A property
inherited unchanged is the same object on both sides; it is equal to
itself at once. CustomProperty::operator== was 1.6% of the Web process's
busy time on GitHub on IRIX.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/Source/WebCore/style/StyleCustomProperty.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/style/StyleCustomProperty.cpp
@@ -46,6 +46,11 @@
 
 bool CustomProperty::operator==(const CustomProperty& other) const
 {
+    // The same property (inherited unchanged, shared by both sides of a
+    // custom property set comparison): equal without a look at its value.
+    if (this == &other)
+        return true;
+
     if (m_name != other.m_name || m_value.index() != other.m_value.index())
         return false;
 
